    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0377" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 339.41/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have received a
                    telegram from Sir Edward Grey instructing me to convey the thanks of His
                    Majesty’s Government to the United States Government for the courtesy and good
                    will displayed by them in issuing orders<anchor n="9" xml:id="d370-f1"/> to the
                    United States ship <pb facs="0378" n="262" xml:id="pg262"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Wheeling</hi>, proceeding to Santo Domingo, to protect
                    British subjects as well as American citizens.</p>
                <p>It gives me much pleasure to be the bearer of this message.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi></signed>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S. April 29. I have just heard from your Department that owing to
                        interruption of the cable the <hi rendition="#italic">Petrel</hi> has been
                        sent to Santo Domingo instead of the <hi rendition="#italic">Wheeling</hi>.
                        I have informed Sir E. Grey accordingly.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <signed>C. S. R.</signed>
                    </closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d370-f1" n="9" xml:id="d370-f1-content">
                <p>In pursuance of a telephonic request made by the British Embassy on April 25.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
